 only {1293, 1574, 254} (step_16); these are disjoint, so no chain of \u2264600-unit-spaced hops links them. 303's later event (~53000) occurs after 1293's last event, so it cannot seed a cascade either. Conclusion: no time-respecting, delay-bounded cascade from 303 to 1293.", "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "confounder_control"}]}, "raw_final_response": "```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_61ff44a4\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [303, 1293],\n  \"window\": [37896, 57095],\n  \"confidence\": 0.76,\n  \"narrative\": \"Within [37896,57095] the graph is busy (4668 events, 1851 active nodes, step_01), but node 303 participates in only 2 events and 1293 in only 4 (step_02), so any cascade must run through a very thin set of edges. 303's out-neighbours are {1409, 1465} and 1293's in-neighbours are {28, 1438, 1574} (step_03, step_04) \u2014 disjoint sets. The static 2-hop neighbourhood of 303 (step_05) contains 16 nodes and does not include 1293 or any of its in-neighbours; a static connection only appears at greater depth through the very high-degree hub 28 (step_06), which is a popularity/aggregation confounder rather than temporal evidence. Binary-search localisation of the two nodes' events (step_07\u2013step_14) places 303's activity in [46896,47195] and [52896,53195], while 1293's inbound activity falls at [42696,43895], [45096,46295], [47496,48295] and [52596,52895]. The only ordering that could work is 303's ~47000 event preceding 1293's ~47900 event, but the 600-unit forward cone of 303 from that event contains only {303, 960, 1409} (step_15) and the 600-unit backward cone of 1293 contains only {1293, 1574, 254} (step_16); these are disjoint, so no chain of \u2264600-unit-spaced hops links them. 303's later event (~53000) occurs after 1293's last event, so it cannot seed a cascade either. Conclusion: no time-respecting, delay-bounded cascade from 303 to 1293.\"\n  ,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ]\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 52357, "total_output_tokens": 6682, "total_tokens": 59039, "total_latency_ms": 93647, "llm_calls": 9, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}